# Optional. Most machines never need a mobile/.env.
#
# Without it the app finds the backend by itself, on port 8000:
#   - in a browser, on the machine the page came from (http://localhost:8000/api);
#   - on a phone in Expo Go, on the computer that served the app to the phone.
#
# Copy this file to mobile/.env only when the backend runs somewhere else, then restart Expo.
# For a phone, start the backend with --host 0.0.0.0 and keep the phone and the computer on the
# same network (a phone hotspot works where campus Wi-Fi does not).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.15:8000/api
